    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "研究者为什么需要「ELIZA」？当时已有的方法究竟卡在了哪里？",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "20 世纪 60 年代，AI 语言系统多为手工构建的符号系统。ELIZA 测试少量脚本能否维持自然对话的印象。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-eliza-cacm-paper"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "DOCTOR 脚本并不理解心理治疗；它把识别到的模式转成反问式提示，诱导用户继续说下去。 关键机制是模式匹配与脚本反射，它把资料线索与可见的演示行为连接起来。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-eliza-cacm-paper"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "专家通常认为 ELIZA 既具有历史重要性，也具有警示意义：它没有深层理解，却能制造对话幻觉。它的长期影响在于提醒人们，交互设计、期待和用户投射会强烈影响对 AI 的判断。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-eliza-cacm-paper"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "这条线索还没有结束。接下来来到「SHRDLU」，我们会看到研究者怎样把问题继续向前推进。",
            "sourceIds": [],
